Fix -Werror=return-type build failure and a -Wwrite-strings warning in
Infineon/arduino-optiga-trust-m v1.1.0.

Six pal_status_t functions fell off the end of the function without a return,
which is a hard error under GCC's -Werror=return-type (the rp2040 core enables
it). pal_logger_read is an unimplemented stub with no callers in the library,
so it returns PAL_STATUS_FAILURE; the rest return PAL_STATUS_SUCCESS.
output_result() took char* for what are always string literals.

Apply from the library root:  patch -p1 < 0001-fix-pal-return-types.patch

--- a/src/optiga_trustm/pal_logger_arduino.cpp
+++ b/src/optiga_trustm/pal_logger_arduino.cpp
@@ -61,13 +61,15 @@
 {
   String str = (char*)p_log_data;
 
-  for(int i=0; i< log_data_length; i++) {
+  for(uint32_t i=0; i< log_data_length; i++) {
     Serial.print(str.charAt(i));
   }
+
   return PAL_STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
 
 pal_status_t pal_logger_read(void * p_logger_context, uint8_t * p_log_data, uint32_t log_data_length)
 {
-  return PAL_STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    //Reading back from the log console is not supported on Arduino
+    return PAL_STATUS_FAILURE;
 }
\ No newline at end of file
